WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.020
There was a planet

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.120
it was one of the few planets in it's entire galaxy cluster that contained life

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.220
and one of the even fewer that made it all the way to the first form of conscious life

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:18.520
A Species that descended from a long lineage of inconceivably good fortune comprised of the right traits in the right planetary conditions at the right time

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.280
like a newborn baby opening its eyes for the first time the emergence of this species was opening the eyes of the universe out from the crust of the planet

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.420
They were the first

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.579
organism on the planet to recognize that they were an

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:36.869
organism on a planet not only able to be and feel and sense the material of everything but able to think and wonder and create out of it all

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.040
able to harness the elements of the planet into tools and technologies

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.079
Able to transmute the chemicals of their own biology and demeaning and love and fellowship

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:52.379
They were a product of infinity an anomaly of existence although rich with intelligence and self-awareness

00:00:52.989 --> 00:00:59.909
Although capable of great acts of creation and understanding their bodies and organs remain soft vulnerable and short lived

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:05.429
During the better part of the species initial development individuals lived on average for only 40 years

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.709
Not much longer than anything else on the planet

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.330
In fact shorter than many things at which point their bodies decayed enough to shut down

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.869
Turning off the spotlight of their individual consciousness forever

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:22.289
Not only that but many died early their bodies being a complex fragile and predominantly liquid based system

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.439
Meant that any number of incidents of damage could shut the whole thing down

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:33.509
Furthermore in many cases even if the body went on harm from the outside it still remains susceptible to various diseases that developed internally

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.960
viruses

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:42.899
microorganisms and other materials could take form destroying their bodies from the inside the same consciousness that granted the species their incredible abilities of

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.420
Understanding and art and science and technology

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:52.229
And love and meaning was the same consciousness that made them aware of the fact that they were a consciousness stuck inside an absurd

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.460
fragile short-lived body

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.810
Destined to lose it all

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:01.019
When my perhaps think that the awareness of their mortality would have compelled them to live as if they were going to die

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.569
But for the most part it had the opposite effect

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.699
The knowledge that they were going to die and the expectation of how much time they likely had before they did

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:14.879
Created a horrible friction between how much to focus on the present versus how much on the future which in many cases

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.199
Defaulted into an inertia and many lived as if they would live forever

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.949
rarely appreciating or making the most out of their magnificent position

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:30.179
There was however a phenomenon that seemed to change things and a portion of individuals sometimes a disease or condition would develop

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:37.199
One that could be diagnosed but not sufficiently treated or cured and as a result the individuals life expectancy would reduce

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:44.850
Some of these diseases were slow burning and left the individual with several mostly untainted years left before it did them in. The diseased

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.809
individual would then be forced to live not only with the awareness that they were going to die

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.959
But the awareness that they were going to die sooner than they expected

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.130
Most commonly this would occur in their mid life and typically reduce the individuals life

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.009
expectancy from 40 down to around 20 or

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.040
15 years

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:06.450
whenever this happened for some reason they would often make major changes in their life as if they weren't already living in a way that

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.200
Was suitable for their mortality

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.119
Suddenly they seemed to say more of what they wanted to say do more of what they wanted to do

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.619
Be more of who they wanted to be every moment became immensely more valuable to them

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:23.310
They often slowed down and more frequently appreciated the nature of everything around and in them squeezing all the life out of the life

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.970
they had left even though they were already going to die when their

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.559
Expectations of when was cut down the true shortness of their life suddenly revealed itself

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.360
Five hundred years would go by as a result of technology and medical

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.489
Advancements the species managed to increase the average life expectancy of their bodies to 75 years

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:49.229
The result of a long laborious effort to add more time to their existence. However, their frame of reference and expectation of life's length

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:51.940
simultaneously increased alongside

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.859
35 more years were added but life felt no longer nor shorter to them

00:03:55.989 --> 00:04:01.289
Although there were fewer during this time there still remained plenty of diseases that exceeded the species medical

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:08.549
understanding diseases that could be diagnosed but not sufficiently treated or cured and was shortened the deceased individuals lifespan now, however,

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:14.220
When individuals were diagnosed with these certain diseases and most commonly reduced their lifespans down to their 30s or 40s

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.070
after the diseased individual received the news

00:04:17.639 --> 00:04:19.918
Still had time and were not yet incapacitated

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:24.839
They often began living and thinking and acting differently making major changes in their life

00:04:24.909 --> 00:04:28.649
Even though the length of their now shortened life was just as long if not longer

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.759
Than their ancestors full lives the exact same phenomenon occurred

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.110
400 more years later

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:41.999
Significant further advancements continued in technology and medical understanding and again the average life expectancy of the species increased

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:46.109
This time to 273 years old on average again

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:51.360
However, their frame of reference their expectations of how long life lasted rose right alongside

00:04:51.909 --> 00:04:53.620
although far less often

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:59.819
individuals of this time period still experienced uncurable conditions and diseases which shortened their lifespans now, however,

00:04:59.819 --> 00:05:03.539
It would more typically only be as low as 70 or 80 years old

00:05:03.699 --> 00:05:10.109
But of course the phenomenon still occurred when individuals received the news that they would likely only live until their 70s or 80s

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:18.689
Suddenly life became incredibly short they began living and thinking and acting differently often making major changes in their life

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:24.689
this continued on and on into the future every time the species added more time to their life their

00:05:24.939 --> 00:05:26.939
expectations of how long life should be

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:33.088
Neutralized their perception of it being any longer no matter what number the life expectancy was. It was always to be expected

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.919
And what was to be expected? It didn't feel long nor short no matter how it felt though

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:38.710
Of course

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:43.859
It was always short whether it was one year or a thousand both were fractions of fractions

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:50.219
Of a microscopic blip of eternity and it was only those who realized that the true measurement of life was not the length

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:53.309
But the depth that ever really changed how it felt

